[00:00:04] Clara Vogel: Let's start. Three items today: the Halden approach, the restructuring options and the timeline to the end of the year.
[00:00:20] Niklas Roth: I will go through the Halden numbers first. Halden Bikes GmbH in Hamburg is a competitor of about our size, and their sales are concentrated in the same dealers we work with in DE.
[00:00:41] Mia Janssen: Before the numbers, what is the cash position if we do this? I need that for the November plan.
[00:00:52] Niklas Roth: The cash case holds on the base case. The deal itself is a possible acquisition of competitor Halden Bikes GmbH (Hamburg) for up to EUR 11M, so the price is the thing to watch.
[00:01:10] Clara Vogel: Good. Next, the restructuring. The idea is to merge Amsterdam and Halden sales into one team, so we do not run two sales teams in the same cities. The restructuring plan is: merge Amsterdam and Halden sales, 8 roles at risk.
[00:01:27] Mia Janssen: That means roles change in Amsterdam. Do we have a number for that?
[00:01:33] Niklas Roth: That is 8 roles at risk across both sales teams in the base case. Hannah will confirm the split by function.
[00:01:52] Clara Vogel: We need to be honest about the risk, so the eight roles stay in the paper as a range, not a promise. Mia, can HR model the notice periods?
[00:02:06] Mia Janssen: Yes. Hannah has the notice period table from the last round. I will ask her to send me a version for each option.
[00:02:18] Niklas Roth: There is a second option. We could keep both sales teams and close the Amsterdam design studio instead, which saves less but keeps the sales structure.
[00:02:34] Clara Vogel: I do not want to close the design studio unless we have no other route. The rider experience depends on it. Let's keep it as the second option in the deck.
[00:02:50] Mia Janssen: Agreed. The design studio stays in the paper as an option, not a recommendation.
[00:03:02] Niklas Roth: The timeline in the deck runs to 15 December. That is the date for the board decision and the date for the first legal steps.
[00:03:15] Clara Vogel: Then the timeline is firm. We will not tell staff anything about the acquisition or the restructuring before 15 December.
[00:03:24] Mia Janssen: Then we need a clear line for the all-hands, so nobody is surprised and nobody gets false answers.
[00:03:34] Clara Vogel: Right. Staff hear that leadership is reviewing how we are organised, and that details will come when there is something to share. Nothing more until the board decides.
[00:03:52] Niklas Roth: I can draft that line for the all-hands and send it to you tonight. It will not name Halden or the roles.
[00:04:05] Clara Vogel: Good. Risks next. Niklas, what could make the deal fail?
[00:04:12] Niklas Roth: Three things. The Halden owners want a higher price, the dealer overlap creates customer loss in the merger period, and the staff side could make the restructuring slower than planned.
[00:04:31] Mia Janssen: On dealer loss, we should ask Elena for a list of the dealers at risk before anything moves. She knows the overlap better than the deck does.
[00:04:45] Clara Vogel: Agreed. Keep the list small and do not send it outside this group.
[00:04:53] Niklas Roth: I will prepare that. Anything else for the paper?
[00:04:58] Clara Vogel: No. Thank you both. We reconvene on 10 November to decide the next step on the deal.
